  "problem": "${f}^{\u2032}(x)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $[$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y]$",
  "worked_solution": "For our scalar function, we have that\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)={(\u2207f)}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x} & \\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEarlier, we found that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}=-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y.\n$$\n\nThe partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(-{y}^{4}-5{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+10{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}+2)=-10x{y}^{2}-4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,-10x{y}^{2}-4x\\, & \\,-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
